WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.203
President Trump gave yet another

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:06.239
unhinged performance
at a campaign rally on Saturday.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.808
And his education secretary
followed up the next day

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.477
by giving a train wreck of
an interview to "60 Minutes."

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:13.680
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.148
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.516 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:20.787
With the Stormy Daniels story
gaining traction every day

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.822
and the Russia investigation
intensifying,

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.658
maybe Trump is under
an unusual amount of stress

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:29.061
because on Saturday, he flew
to Pennsylvania to rally for

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:31.831
the Republican candidate in a
special Congressional election,

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.199
and even by his standards,

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.701
Trump's antics were especially
off the rails.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.237
Now, as for the candidate,
Rick Saccone,

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:42.475
who Trump was ostensibly there
to support, he barely came up.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.910
Trump's like the friend
you invite

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.377
to your karaoke birthday party

00:00:45.377 --> 00:00:46.846
who shows up late,
doesn't bring a gift,

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.214
and then sings
"Stairway to Heaven"

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.549
10 times in a row.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.617
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.652
And Trump was playing
all the hits,

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.255
reeling off vulgar insults
of reporters and politicians

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.755
by name, like, for example,

00:00:56.755 --> 00:00:59.291
when he brought up the prospect
of running against Oprah

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.527
and implied that he knew
something about her

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.129
that the public does not.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.664
-Wouldn't we love to run
against Oprah?

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.698
I would love it.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:06.366
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.900
I would love it.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.669
That would be a painful
experience for her.

00:01:10.669 --> 00:01:12.105
Oh, I'd love Oprah to win.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.172
I'd love to beat Oprah.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.273
I know her weakness.

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:15.241
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.042
No, no, I know her weakness.

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:18.545
-I know her weakness?

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.945
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:22.882
He talks about Oprah the way
Lex Luthor talks about Superman.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.983
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.551
And you're not special.

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:28.020
We all know her weakness.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.456
-I love bread.

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.225
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:35.628
-And listen,

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.397
don't think you can stop her
just because you look like

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:39.766
the Pillsbury Doughboy.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.203
And that's it.
That's Oprah's only weakness.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.705
This is a woman who spent
30 years getting celebrities

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:47.773
to cry on television.

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:49.843
She broke Lance Armstrong.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.577
If Trump ever does debate Oprah,

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:52.678
there's a good chance
it will end

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:54.347
with him sobbing at the podium.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:57.750
[ As Trump ] "You know, you know
who I wish they'd lock up?

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.719
The part of me that's sad."

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.354
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:04.623
[ Normal voice ] But, of course,
Trump was not merely content

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:06.626
to attack one black woman
in his rant.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.429
He then went after California
congresswoman Maxine Waters

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.098
specifically by insulting
her intelligence.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:15.468
-We have to defeat Nancy Pelosi.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:20.707
[ Crowd boos ]

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:23.443
And Maxine Waters,

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:27.213
a very low I.Q. Individual.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.350
-I don't know.
I bet she says "I.Q." faster.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.683
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:33.686
[ As Trump ] "I...Q."

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:37.089
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:38.691
[ Normal voice ]
And Trump knows --

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.827
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:44.330
You guys, Trump knows
high I.Q. individuals,

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.966
like his Secretary of Education
Betsy DeVos,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:51.003
seen here crushing it last night
on "60 Minutes."

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:53.706
-Have the public schools
in Michigan gotten better?

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.775
-I don't know. Overall,

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:58.578
I can't say overall that
they have all gotten better.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.614
-Your argument that if you
take funds away,

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:04.650
that the schools will get better
is not working in Michigan.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:09.822
Where you have a huge impact
and influence over the direction

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:10.756
of the school system here.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:12.324
-I hesitate to talk about

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:14.527
all schools in general

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.562
because schools are made up

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.831
of individual students
attending them.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.899
-Have you seen
the really bad schools?

00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:23.702
Maybe try to figure out what --
what they're doing?

00:03:23.702 --> 00:03:25.404
-I have not. I have not.

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:27.906
I've not intentionally
visited schools

00:03:27.906 --> 00:03:29.541
that are underperforming.

00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:31.978
-Maybe you should.
-Maybe I should.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:35.547
-F-minus. F-minus.

00:03:35.547 --> 00:03:38.117
She's the highest ranking
education official

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.920
in the country, and she acts
like a substitute teacher

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.223
who is just realizing her U.S.
history isn't up to speed.

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:45.424
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:47.393
"Can anyone tell me what this
is a picture of?"

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.962
"Yeah, it's George Washington
crossing the Delaware."

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:52.098
"Well, no, because Delaware
is a state.

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:53.433
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.267
So you wouldn't need a boat
to cross it."

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.902
"Yeah, it's also a river."

00:03:56.902 --> 00:03:58.037
"I don't know."

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.238
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.140
"Yeah, it is.
Maybe you should look it up."

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.078
"Yeah. Maybe I should."

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.579
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.347
Now Trump always --

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:10.850
[ Applause ]

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.318
Trump always insults

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.053
and degrades people
at these rallies.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.655
But his performance on Saturday
was especially manic and vulgar.

00:04:16.655 --> 00:04:19.425
For example, Trump started
ranting about his decision

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.460
to meet with North Korean leader
Kim Jong-un.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.629
And when referencing an
interview he gave years ago

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.332
on "Meet the Press" said this
about host Chuck Todd.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.534
-It's 1999.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.870
I'm on "Meet the Press,"

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.037
a show now headed

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:34.740
by Sleepy Eyes Chuck Todd.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.143
He's a sleeping son of a bitch,

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.510
I'll tell you.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.714
-You're calling Chuck Todd
a son of a bitch?

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.417
Seriously, you know someone's
not a son of a bitch

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.285
when they still come off
as approachable

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:49.422
despite having the exact same
facial hair as Evil Spock.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:51.023
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:53.226
Trump is, of course, so obsessed
with earning the praise

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.426
and validation of the media,

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:56.095
that at one point during
his rant on North Korea,

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.497
he literally just started
rambling nonsensically

00:04:58.497 --> 00:04:59.965
about President Obama,

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:02.568
claiming Obama would not have
been able to arrange a meeting

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:03.803
with Kim Jong-un.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.538
-They're saying not
that big a deal,

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.438
anybody could have done it.

00:05:06.438 --> 00:05:07.740
Obama could have done it.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.542
Obama had a chance --
[ Crowd boos ]

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:13.112
No, no. They're saying -- Obama.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.915
Obama. Obama.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.616
-Just --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:21.119
Just mumbling Obama's name
like --

00:05:21.119 --> 00:05:23.990
like Obama was the name
of his childhood sled.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.691
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:27.726
His presidential diaries
are going to look like

00:05:27.726 --> 00:05:29.529
the manuscript
from "The Shining."

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.864
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.732
Of course, one major difference
between Obama and Trump

00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:35.935
is that for Trump the presidency
isn't actually a job,

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.303
it's just a performance.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.438
And on Saturday, he defended
his performance by playing

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:41.507
make-believe onstage
and acting out

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.442
what it would be like
if he were less unhinged

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:45.177
and more subdued as president.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:46.345
-You know how easy -- remember

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:47.680
I used to say how easy it is

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.048
to be presidential?

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.516
But you'd all be out of here
right now if I --

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.251
you'd be so bored.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.919
Because I could stand up, right?

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:57.089
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:57.089 --> 00:06:00.792
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.792 --> 00:06:03.129
I'm very presidential.

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.296
[ Deep voice ]
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:06.199
thank you for being here
tonight.

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:10.069
And then you go, "God bless you,

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:13.639
and God bless the United States
of America."

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.240
Thank you very much.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:19.111
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.814
-I have to say, he might be
the only white comedian

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.382
who does a white guy voice.

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:25.985
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:35.094
He's pretty [bleep] funny
sometimes.

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:37.162
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:38.731
But Trump's ranting about
North Korea

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.132
and being presidential
tells us a lot

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:42.301
about his shock announcement
last week that he had agreed

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.170
to a summit meeting
with Kim Jong-un.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.538
Now it's undeniably better
to be on a path toward peace

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:48.140
than a ramp-up to war.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:51.043
And if Trump somehow manages
to fall ass-backwards

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:53.112
into a peaceful resolution
with North Korea,

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:55.447
then that is absolutely
a good thing.

00:06:55.447 --> 00:06:57.283
And if that happens,
I will be the first to admit,

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:59.284
okay, he wasn't Darth Vader,

00:06:59.284 --> 00:07:01.921
he was Mr. Bean.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:05.290
But for Trump, this is as usual
mostly about the show,

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.293
not about the policy because
for months,

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:10.429
he's repeatedly insisted that
diplomacy was not the answer

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:13.165
and even as late as last week,
he was incredibly vague

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:16.235
about whether he favored
negotiation or military action.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.304
-President Trump tweeted,
and I quote...

00:07:33.185 --> 00:07:35.320
-We sent out through social
media statement

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.555
willing to go either way.

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:37.589
Hopefully it's going to be

00:07:37.589 --> 00:07:38.356
the proper way.

00:07:38.356 --> 00:07:39.558
The proper way is the way

00:07:39.558 --> 00:07:41.060
that everybody knows

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.795
and everybody wants.

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.930
-Wow. You are so clear
and well spoken.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.032
Who was your teacher?
Betsy DeVos?

00:07:47.032 --> 00:07:49.468
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:49.468 --> 00:07:55.107
So, Trump kept --
kept batting down

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:57.009
his own Secretary of State's
attempts to secure

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.211
a peaceful resolution
even when asked point blank

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:01.914
what he would do was incredibly
vague because, of course,

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:03.449
he had no idea what he would do.

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:05.151
It was only after
careful diplomacy

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:07.720
that South Korea was able
to make this breakthrough,

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.057
Trump caring only about the
spectacle accepted on the spot,

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:13.025
while Congressional leaders
and top officials

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:14.426 line:0%
at the Pentagon
and State Department

00:08:14.426 --> 00:08:16.362 line:0%
learned what was happening
from news reports.

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:17.797
So the Pentagon
and State Department

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:20.399
have to watch the news to find
out what the President is doing.

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.668
I guess it's not surprising
since the President

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:25.338
also watches the news to find
out what the President's doing.

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:26.572
[ Applause ]

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:30.409
In fact, even --
even the way Trump notified

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:31.610
the press about the news

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.879
was more about theater
than substance.

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:36.415
After the South Koreans
relayed the invitation,

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:38.350
Trump walked over
to the White House briefing room

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.552
and teased reporters with
a vague announcement.

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:42.221
-Within the last few moments,

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:44.256
President Trump stuck his head

00:08:44.256 --> 00:08:45.057
into the White House

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:47.459
briefing room and said that

00:08:47.459 --> 00:08:48.994
there would be a major
announcement

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:50.730
coming this evening.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:51.730
-And I said, "Mr. President,

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.666
what is the announcement
going to be on?"

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.968
And he said, "North Korea."

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:57.002
-We're showing our viewers

00:08:57.002 --> 00:08:59.505
a picture when he simply walked

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:01.073
into the briefing room over

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:02.441
there, the press briefing room.

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:04.576
-Okay, first of all,
you can't just pop in,

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:07.913
say you've got big news
on North Korea, and leave.

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:10.316
That's like your doctor
peeking into your exam room

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:12.784
and saying, "I just
got your test results back,

00:09:12.784 --> 00:09:14.520
and they are crazy!"

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:15.887
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.887 --> 00:09:17.323
Seriously, though, look at him.

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:19.925
He looks like he's popping
his head into the break room

00:09:19.925 --> 00:09:21.527
to see if there's
any pizza left.

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:22.728
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:24.663
[ As Trump ] "You guys,
big news on North Korea.

00:09:24.663 --> 00:09:26.232
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:28.100
You guys eat all the pizza?"

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.635
[ Normal voice ] But Trump
made his priorities clear

00:09:29.635 --> 00:09:30.836
when he spoke to reporters
Thursday.

00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:32.238
He didn't comment
on the substance

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:33.906
of the announcement
or how it would work.

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:36.776
His focus was mainly about how
the press would report on it.

00:09:36.776 --> 00:09:39.144
-He was almost giddy about this,

00:09:39.144 --> 00:09:40.813
ecstatic about this news.

00:09:40.813 --> 00:09:42.348
He said that this

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:43.649
would be a big development.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:45.217
I asked if it was about
negotiations.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:47.553
He said says it's almost
beyond that and then he said,

00:09:47.553 --> 00:09:49.889
"I hope you give me credit."

00:09:49.889 --> 00:09:51.123
-That's all he cares about.

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:53.092
He just wants credit
unless things go wrong,

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:54.660
then he wants to avoid blame.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.862
If he meets with Kim Jong-un
and it's a disaster,

00:09:56.862 --> 00:09:58.496
you know who who
he'll blame it on.

00:09:58.496 --> 00:10:02.401
-Obama. Obama. Obama.

00:10:02.401 --> 00:10:05.171
-So the President is ranting
nonsensically at rallies

00:10:05.171 --> 00:10:06.505
and his Education Secretary

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:08.707
is giving incomprehensible
answers about education,

00:10:08.707 --> 00:10:11.009
all while the White House
tries to resolve

00:10:11.009 --> 00:10:12.844
a tense situation
with North Korea.

00:10:12.844 --> 00:10:14.680
If Trump manages to stumble
his way into

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.015
a diplomatic breakthrough,

00:10:16.015 --> 00:10:17.983
that would undoubtedly
be a great thing.

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:19.752
But if that happens,
he will have done it

00:10:19.752 --> 00:10:21.119
despite being a very...

00:10:21.119 --> 00:10:23.755
-Low I.Q. individual.

00:10:23.755 --> 00:10:25.424
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:25.424 --> 00:10:26.692
